# Authoritative DNS for the run-recon benchmark lab (RFC 6761 `.test` names only).
# Pass it to run-recon with  --resolvers lab/resolvers.txt  so dnsx/httpx/tlsx
# resolve the lab and farm vhosts (run-recon's built-in public resolvers can't).
#
# Zone files are generated by `bench-run-recon.sh up` (BIND's db.<zone> naming):
#   db.test             every lab/farm name, plus fixtures:
#     A     every lab/farm name   -> 127.0.0.1 (the Caddy ingress, loopback-published)
#     AAAA  nginx.test, wp.test   -> 2001:db8:1::10 (RFC 3849 documentation prefix:
#           never routable, but --ipv6 has a record to report for two hosts only)
#     CNAME alias.test  -> nginx.test       (healthy alias: --takeover must not flag it)
#           orphan.test -> gone.cloud.test  (target does not exist: a dangling CNAME)
#     A     direct.nginx.test -> LAB_ORIGIN_IP, and nginx.test's SPF "ip4:LAB_ORIGIN_IP":
#           the leaked "forgotten origin" that --origin must find and verify
#     test. itself is unsigned and refuses zone transfers (--zone-exposure negative case)
#   db.walk.test.signed walk.test signed with NSEC (ldnsutils): the chain can be walked
#   db.xfr.test         xfr.test, unsigned, zone transfers allowed to anyone
# No NSEC3 zone: CoreDNS's file plugin cannot serve one (the suite covers NSEC3 with mocks).
# The file plugin reloads a zone when its serial changes; the reload plugin picks
# up edits to this Corefile, so neither needs a DNS restart.
walk.test:53 {
    file /lab/db.walk.test.signed {
        reload 2s
    }
    errors
}
xfr.test:53 {
    file /lab/db.xfr.test {
        reload 2s
    }
    transfer {
        to *
    }
    errors
}
test:53 {
    file /lab/db.test {
        reload 2s
    }
    reload 2s
    errors
}
